sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-16> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Linear-moving Anthrobots show higher bilateral symmetry of cilia distribution about their axis of movement than circular movers; for circular bots, but not linear bots, the 90-degree rotated axis is more symmetric than the movement axis (p = 0.048), supporting distinct local symmetry profiles for distinct movement types.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Linear-moving Anthrobots are more bilaterally symmetric about their movement axis";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Results › Anthrobots Show Bilateral Asymmetry Along Movement Axis”. Scope: 28 displacing NHBE-derived Anthrobots (15 circular, 13 linear)"
}
